# The kama compiler kyoten builds with: .kama-pin/ (git-ignored), made from a CLEAN clone of kama at the commit below,
# the binary beside the lib/, include/ and prelude/ it was built with. tools/kama runs it and warns when the compiler
# it runs is another. AGENTS.kyoten.md § Build has the recipe; a bump is a commit of its own, made with every suite
# green on the new compiler and nothing else changed.
#
# Windows (msys2 UCRT64), 2026-11-08: first pin, 0.9.886 (2159ce21), at the owner's direction that kyoten keep its own
# copy because ../kama rebuilds as it develops on this machine (it moved 0.9.877 -> 0.9.881 -> 0.9.884 in one session).
# Before it, steps 4 to 5.2 were built on ../kama's working binary: 0.9.876, then 0.9.881+g4267d2ec.
#
# 2026-11-09: 0.9.886 -> 0.9.899 (f32373ea), kama's dev HEAD with a clean tree. What moved, for kyoten:
#   0.9.893 KR-357 (KY-41, KY-42): isize and usize at the target's width at compile time.
#   0.9.894 KR-358 (KY-46): `T.default()` is an operand, so `Id.second() != Id.default()` builds.
#   0.9.895 KR-359 (KY-43): the strict reader refuses a key the object already gave, naming its path.
#   0.9.896 (KY-47): InlineDynamicArray's length is an int32, one size on every target.
#   0.9.897 KR-360 (KY-39, KY-44): a query names each type's declaration (`path`), says whether a symbol is
#           `exported`, and reads an elected ctor as `default ctor`.
#   Also 0.9.887-0.9.892 (Xtensa atomics, a wasm program that spawns compiles with -pthread, parallel_for on the job
#   pool, a sub-int operation beside an unsuffixed literal takes the operand's type) and 0.9.898-0.9.899 (fibers on
#   Windows), none of which kyoten uses. Green on it with no other change: tools/test.sh (engine 114 cases native debug,
#   release and wasm; the frame guard; the tool's 117; fps native and wasm; vr checked), @kama/window's (36 native,
#   20 under node) and @kama/gpu's (3 cases, the clear example's 60 frames, the xfail, the wasm build).
KAMA_VERSION=0.9.899
KAMA_BUILD=gf32373ea
